('79676da2-222f-5250-9d6d-3617e2f2a1e9','44375a14-adfc-50ae-9650-2d8b5d3737da',3,'idiom','B2',null,null,null,'[]'::jsonb),
('c4b9d77e-dd41-5f5a-a16b-c8d5fa68ff86','3a0ca70b-bdd5-5309-a96e-6faef05fa84e',1,'noun','A1','S1','W1','[ countable ]','[{"phrase":"face to face","register":null,"definition_en":"a face-to-face meeting , conversation etc is one where you are with another person and talking to them","translation":"ملاقات حضوری، مکالمه و غیره جایی است که شما با شخص دیگری هستید و با او صحبت می کنید","example":"a face-to-face interview","example_translation":"مصاحبه حضوری","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638215.mp3"},{"phrase":"on the face of it","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that something seems true but that you think there may be other facts about it which are not yet clear","translation":"می گفت که چیزی درست به نظر می رسد اما فکر می کنید ممکن است حقایق دیگری در مورد آن وجود داشته باشد که هنوز روشن نیست","example":"It looks, on the face of it, like a minor change in the regulations.","example_translation":"ظاهراً به نظر یک تغییر جزئی در مقررات است.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204510.mp3"},{"phrase":"the face of something","register":null,"definition_en":"the nature or character of an organization, industry , system etc, and the way it appears to people","translation":"ماهیت یا شخصیت یک سازمان، صنعت، سیستم و غیره و نحوه ظاهر شدن آن برای مردم","example":"technology that has changed the face of society","example_translation":"فناوری که چهره جامعه را تغییر داده است","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204517.mp3"},{"phrase":"lose face","register":null,"definition_en":"if you lose face, you do something which makes you seem weak , stupid etc, and which makes people respect you less","translation":"اگر چهره خود را از دست بدهید، کاری انجام می دهید که شما را ضعیف، احمق و غیره نشان می دهد و باعث می شود مردم کمتر به شما احترام بگذارند.","example":"He doesn’t want to back down (= accept defeat in an argument ) and risk losing face.","example_translation":"او نمی‌خواهد عقب‌نشینی کند (= قبول شکست در یک بحث) و خطر از دست دادن چهره.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204526.mp3"},{"phrase":"on the face of the earth","register":null,"definition_en":"used when you are emphasizing a statement to mean ‘in the whole world’","translation":"زمانی استفاده می شود که بر یک جمله به معنای \"در تمام دنیا\" تاکید می کنید.","example":"If she were the last woman on the face of the earth, I still wouldn’t be interested!","example_translation":"اگر او آخرین زن روی زمین بود، باز هم علاقه ای نداشتم!","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000550.mp3"},{"phrase":"get out of my face","register":"spoken","definition_en":"used to tell someone in an impolite way to go away because they are annoying you","translation":"به طور غیر مودبانه ای به کسی میگفت برو برو چون اذیتت میکنه","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"put your face on","register":"informal","definition_en":"to put make-up on","translation":"برای آرایش کردن","example":"I just need to run upstairs and put my face on.","example_translation":"فقط باید بروم بالا و صورتم را بپوشم.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638120.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0','3a0ca70b-bdd5-5309-a96e-6faef05fa84e',2,'verb','A1','S1','W1','[ transitive ]','[{"phrase":"face the music","register":"informal","definition_en":"to accept criticism or punishment for something you have done","translation":"پذیرفتن انتقاد یا تنبیه برای کاری که انجام داده اید","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""}]'::jsonb),
('78e6ed5a-994c-5f2a-a81b-44dbeb04fc40','d593ba7b-9ee5-5381-8590-50b06122bb08',1,'noun','A1','S1','W1',null,'[{"phrase":"the fact remains","register":null,"definition_en":"used to emphasize that what you are saying about a situation is true and people must realize this","translation":"برای تاکید بر اینکه آنچه شما در مورد یک موقعیت می گویید درست است و مردم باید این را درک کنند","example":"The fact remains that the number of homeless people is rising daily.","example_translation":"واقعیت این است که تعداد افراد بی خانمان هر روز در حال افزایش است.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206655.mp3"},{"phrase":"facts and figures","register":null,"definition_en":"the basic details , numbers etc concerning a particular situation or subject","translation":"جزئیات اساسی، اعداد و غیره در مورد یک موقعیت یا موضوع خاص","example":"Here are a few facts and figures about the country.","example_translation":"در اینجا چند واقعیت و آمار در مورد این کشور آورده شده است.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638276.mp3"},{"phrase":"the facts speak for themselves","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that the things that have happened or the things someone has done show clearly that something is true","translation":"می گفت چیزهایی که اتفاق افتاده یا کارهایی که کسی انجام داده است به وضوح نشان می دهد که چیزی درست است","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"after the fact","register":null,"definition_en":"after something has happened or been done, especially after a mistake has been made","translation":"بعد از اینکه چیزی اتفاق افتاده یا انجام شده است، به ویژه پس از انجام یک اشتباه","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""}]'::jsonb),
('27d9abdf-39af-5821-a9ee-7a39c231b8ff','b5e2e6e4-ec69-5b75-a0c4-b43dadf3d1fb',1,'verb','A2','S2','W1',null,'[{"phrase":"never fail to do something","register":null,"definition_en":"to do something or happen so regularly that people expect it","translation":"انجام کاری یا اتفاقی به قدری منظم که مردم انتظار آن را دارند","example":"My grandson never fails to phone me on my birthday.","example_translation":"نوه ام هرگز در روز تولدم با من تماس نمی گیرد.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001207303.mp3"},{"phrase":"fail somebody","register":null,"definition_en":"to not do what someone has trusted you to do","translation":"کاری را انجام ندهید که کسی به شما اعتماد کرده است","example":"I feel I’ve failed my children by not spending more time with them.","example_translation":"احساس می‌کنم فرزندانم را با صرف نکردن وقت بیشتر با آنها شکست داده‌ام.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001207313.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('5919246d-0814-51f6-8689-b9f7f48a2fd5','b5e2e6e4-ec69-5b75-a0c4-b43dadf3d1fb',2,'noun','A2',null,null,null,'[{"phrase":"without fail","register":null,"definition_en":"if you do something without fail , you always do it","translation":"اگر کاری را بدون شکست انجام دهید، همیشه آن را انجام می دهید","example":"Tim visits his mother every day without fail.","example_translation":"تیم هر روز بدون شکست به دیدن مادرش می رود.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001208675.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('1ed8fdd8-1287-52f1-94e7-efc19643e535','b5e2e6e4-ec69-5b75-a0c4-b43dadf3d1fb',3,'interjection','A2',null,null,null,'[]'::jsonb),
('6042235a-fc8a-5fea-a22c-16eefdad2060','aac3838d-4cd9-57d3-9859-90c5d22eb6e8',1,'adjective','A2','S1','W2',null,'[{"phrase":"give somebody a fair crack of the whip","register":"informal","definition_en":"to give someone the opportunity to do something, especially so that they can show that they are able to do it","translation":"به کسی فرصت انجام کاری را بدهند، مخصوصاً تا بتواند نشان دهد که قادر به انجام آن کار است","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"by fair means or foul","register":null,"definition_en":"using any method to get what you want, including dishonest or illegal methods","translation":"از هر روشی برای رسیدن به آنچه می خواهید استفاده کنید، از جمله روش های غیر صادقانه یا غیرقانونی","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"fair enough","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that you agree with someone’s suggestion or that something seems reasonable","translation":"می گفت که شما با پیشنهاد کسی موافق هستید یا چیزی معقول به نظر می رسد","example":"‘I think we should split the bill.’ ‘Fair enough.’","example_translation":"«فکر می‌کنم باید صورت‌حساب را تقسیم کنیم.» «به اندازه کافی منصفانه است.»","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209022.mp3"},{"phrase":"to be fair","register":null,"definition_en":"used when adding something after someone has been criticized , which helps to explain or excuse what they did","translation":"هنگام اضافه کردن چیزی بعد از انتقاد از کسی استفاده می شود، که به توضیح یا توجیه کاری که انجام داده است کمک می کند","example":"She should have phoned to tell us what her plans were although, to be fair, she’s been very busy.","example_translation":"او باید تلفن می‌کرد تا به ما بگوید برنامه‌هایش چیست، اگرچه، انصافاً، او بسیار شلوغ بود.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209036.mp3"},{"phrase":"fair comment","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that a remark or criticism seems reasonable","translation":"قبلاً می گفت که یک اظهار نظر یا انتقاد منطقی به نظر می رسد","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"with your own fair hands","register":null,"definition_en":"if you do something with your own fair hands , you do it yourself without any help – used humorously","translation":"اگر کاری را با دستان منصفانه خود انجام دهید، خودتان آن را بدون هیچ کمکی انجام می دهید - به صورت طنز استفاده می شود","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""}]'::jsonb),
('05b22a6f-41f8-5255-9f09-9c6657b827a4','aac3838d-4cd9-57d3-9859-90c5d22eb6e8',2,'noun','A2',null,null,'[ countable ]','[]'::jsonb),
('b277217c-eea6-550e-b6e4-e205cd57de24','aac3838d-4cd9-57d3-9859-90c5d22eb6e8',3,'adverb','A2','S2','W3',null,'[{"phrase":"play fair","register":null,"definition_en":"to do something in a fair and honest way","translation":"انجام کاری به شیوه ای منصفانه و صادقانه","example":"In international trade, very few countries play fair.","example_translation":"در تجارت بین الملل، کشورهای بسیار کمی منصفانه بازی می کنند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638458.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('0fd6f194-e636-5d0d-846b-c5ee83474be9','a9f2512a-dd33-5c43-84cf-ac6d7a49e54d',1,'verb','A1','S1','W1','( past tense fell / fel / , past participle fallen / ˈfɔːlən $ ˈfɒːl- / )','[{"phrase":"fall short of something","register":null,"definition_en":"to be less than the amount or standard that is needed or that you want","translation":"کمتر از مقدار یا استاندارد مورد نیاز یا مورد نظر شما باشد","example":"This year’s profit will fall short of 13%.","example_translation":"سود امسال کمتر از 13 درصد خواهد بود.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209770.mp3"},{"phrase":"fall into place","register":null,"definition_en":"if parts of a situation that you have been trying to understand fall into place, you start to understand how they are connected with each other","translation":"اگر بخش‌هایی از موقعیتی که سعی کرده‌اید بفهمید در جای خود قرار می‌گیرند، شروع به درک نحوه ارتباط آنها با یکدیگر می‌کنید","example":"Suddenly, all the details started falling into place.","example_translation":"ناگهان، تمام جزئیات شروع به در هم ریختن کردند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001791232.mp3"},{"phrase":"fall flat","register":null,"definition_en":"if a joke , remark , or performance falls flat , it fails to interest or amuse people","translation":"اگر یک شوخی، اظهار نظر یا اجرا بی نتیجه باشد، باعث علاقه یا سرگرم کردن مردم نمی شود.","example":"Marlow’s attempts at jokes fell flat.","example_translation":"تلاش مارلو برای شوخی بی نتیجه ماند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001791252.mp3"},{"phrase":"fall by the wayside","register":null,"definition_en":"to fail , or to stop being done, used, or made","translation":"شکست خوردن، یا متوقف کردن انجام، استفاده یا ساخته شدن","example":"Health reform was one of his goals that fell by the wayside.","example_translation":"اصلاح سلامت یکی از اهداف او بود که به حاشیه رفت.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209846.mp3"},{"phrase":"fall from a great height","register":null,"definition_en":"to be forced to leave an important job or position , or lose the respect that people had for you","translation":"مجبور شوید یک شغل یا موقعیت مهم را ترک کنید یا احترامی را که مردم برای شما قائل بودند از دست بدهید","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"fall into step","register":null,"definition_en":"to start to walk next to someone else, at the same speed as them","translation":"شروع به راه رفتن در کنار شخص دیگری، با همان سرعت او","example":"Holly slowed her pace and fell into step with the old man.","example_translation":"هالی سرعت خود را کم کرد و با پیرمرد همگام شد.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001791280.mp3"},{"phrase":"fall into line","register":null,"definition_en":"to obey someone or do what other people want you to do, especially when you do not want to do it at first","translation":"از کسی اطاعت کنید یا کاری را انجام دهید که دیگران از شما می خواهند، به خصوص زمانی که در ابتدا نمی خواهید آن را انجام دهید","example":"Most countries have signed the treaty but some are reluctant to fall into line.","example_translation":"اکثر کشورها این معاهده را امضا کرده اند، اما برخی از آنها تمایلی به همسویی ندارند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001791291.mp3"},{"phrase":"fall between two stools","register":null,"definition_en":"to be neither one type of thing nor another, or be unable to choose between two ways of doing something","translation":"اینکه نه یک نوع کار باشد و نه نوع دیگر، یا اینکه قادر به انتخاب بین دو روش انجام کاری نباشیم","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"fall on stony ground","register":null,"definition_en":"if a request , suggestion , joke etc falls on stony ground , it is ignored or people do not like it","translation":"اگر درخواست، پیشنهاد، شوخی و غیره بر روی زمین سنگی بیفتد، نادیده گرفته می شود یا مردم آن را دوست ندارند.","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""}]'::jsonb),
('29bc9abc-eeec-5f11-a0e1-16b3976ce0e8','a9f2512a-dd33-5c43-84cf-ac6d7a49e54d',2,'noun','A1','S2','W2',null,'[{"phrase":"fall from grace","register":null,"definition_en":"a situation in which someone stops being respected by other people or loses their position of authority , especially because they have done something wrong","translation":"موقعیتی که در آن شخص دیگر مورد احترام دیگران قرار نمی گیرد یا موقعیت اقتدار خود را از دست می دهد، به ویژه به این دلیل که کار اشتباهی انجام داده است.","example":"He was the head of the intelligence service until his fall from grace.","example_translation":"او تا زمان سقوطش رئیس سازمان اطلاعات بود.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001210361.mp3"},{"phrase":"the Fall","register":null,"definition_en":"the occasion in the Bible when God punished Adam and Eve by making them leave the Garden of Eden","translation":"مناسبتی در کتاب مقدس که خداوند آدم و حوا را با ترک باغ عدن مجازات کرد","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""}]'::jsonb),
