('e3390650-b524-57c5-b83a-075f4116e016','1382e53d-98bd-5eca-b5b3-c5938b8a6966',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a sum of money that a person or organization owes','[ countable ]',null,'بدهی، دین؛ طلب (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have debts Fortunately, I have no debts.','run up debts ( also amass debts formal ) (= borrow more and more money ) At that time he was drinking a lot and running up debts.','pay off a debt (= pay the money back ) The first thing I''m going to do is pay off my debts.','repay/settle a debt formal (= pay the money back ) He was hoping he would soon have enough money to settle his debts.','clear your debts (= repay all of them ) It took him three years to clear his bank debts.','service a debt (= pay the interest on a debt, but not pay it back ) By then, she was borrowing more money just to service her debts.','write off/cancel a debt (= say officially that it does not have to be paid ) The bank finally agreed to write off the debt.','be burdened with/saddled with debts (= have big debts ) Many poor countries are saddled with huge debts.','reduce a debt The programme aims to reduce the debt of the world''s poorest countries.','big/large The debts got bigger and bigger.','huge (= very big ) Young people often leave university with huge debts.','unpaid/outstanding (= not yet paid ) The average outstanding debt on credit cards in Britain is now over £3,000.','heavy debts (= big debts ) The company wanted to reduce its heavy debts.','a bad debt (= one that is unlikely to be paid back ) Companies lose millions of pounds each year from having to write off bad debts.','a bank debt (= one that you owe to a bank ) The company closed with bank debts of about £350 million.','the national debt (= the total amount that is owed by the government of a country ) Their national debt is the third largest in the world.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She had debts of over £100,000.","translation":"او بیش از 100000 پوند بدهی داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000442.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had enough money to pay off his outstanding debts.","translation":"او پول کافی برای پرداخت بدهی های معوق خود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835003.mp3"},{"sentence":"students who run up huge debts","translation":"دانش آموزانی که بدهی های کلانی دارند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835010.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1014af44-a09b-5b26-8818-8d8b539d4278','1382e53d-98bd-5eca-b5b3-c5938b8a6966',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when you owe money to someone','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی به کسی بدهکار هستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have debts Fortunately, I have no debts.','run up debts ( also amass debts formal ) (= borrow more and more money ) At that time he was drinking a lot and running up debts.','pay off a debt (= pay the money back ) The first thing I''m going to do is pay off my debts.','repay/settle a debt formal (= pay the money back ) He was hoping he would soon have enough money to settle his debts.','clear your debts (= repay all of them ) It took him three years to clear his bank debts.','service a debt (= pay the interest on a debt, but not pay it back ) By then, she was borrowing more money just to service her debts.','write off/cancel a debt (= say officially that it does not have to be paid ) The bank finally agreed to write off the debt.','be burdened with/saddled with debts (= have big debts ) Many poor countries are saddled with huge debts.','reduce a debt The programme aims to reduce the debt of the world''s poorest countries.','big/large The debts got bigger and bigger.','huge (= very big ) Young people often leave university with huge debts.','unpaid/outstanding (= not yet paid ) The average outstanding debt on credit cards in Britain is now over £3,000.','heavy debts (= big debts ) The company wanted to reduce its heavy debts.','a bad debt (= one that is unlikely to be paid back ) Companies lose millions of pounds each year from having to write off bad debts.','a bank debt (= one that you owe to a bank ) The company closed with bank debts of about £350 million.','the national debt (= the total amount that is owed by the government of a country ) Their national debt is the third largest in the world.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Nearly half the students said they were in debt.","translation":"تقریبا نیمی از دانش آموزان گفتند که بدهکار هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684843.mp3"},{"sentence":"The band will be in debt to the record company for years.","translation":"گروه تا سال ها به شرکت ضبط بدهکار خواهد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684846.mp3"},{"sentence":"A rash business decision left him $600 in debt.","translation":"یک تصمیم تجاری عجولانه 600 دلار بدهی برای او به همراه داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835021.mp3"},{"sentence":"The club sank deeper into debt .","translation":"باشگاه بیشتر در بدهی فرو رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835025.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('3f420db6-bcf5-59db-a808-0b3c754dfc14','1382e53d-98bd-5eca-b5b3-c5938b8a6966',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the degree to which you have learned from or been influenced by someone or something else','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'درجه ای که از شخص یا چیز دیگری آموخته اید یا تحت تأثیر آن قرار گرفته اید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have debts Fortunately, I have no debts.','run up debts ( also amass debts formal ) (= borrow more and more money ) At that time he was drinking a lot and running up debts.','pay off a debt (= pay the money back ) The first thing I''m going to do is pay off my debts.','repay/settle a debt formal (= pay the money back ) He was hoping he would soon have enough money to settle his debts.','clear your debts (= repay all of them ) It took him three years to clear his bank debts.','service a debt (= pay the interest on a debt, but not pay it back ) By then, she was borrowing more money just to service her debts.','write off/cancel a debt (= say officially that it does not have to be paid ) The bank finally agreed to write off the debt.','be burdened with/saddled with debts (= have big debts ) Many poor countries are saddled with huge debts.','reduce a debt The programme aims to reduce the debt of the world''s poorest countries.','big/large The debts got bigger and bigger.','huge (= very big ) Young people often leave university with huge debts.','unpaid/outstanding (= not yet paid ) The average outstanding debt on credit cards in Britain is now over £3,000.','heavy debts (= big debts ) The company wanted to reduce its heavy debts.','a bad debt (= one that is unlikely to be paid back ) Companies lose millions of pounds each year from having to write off bad debts.','a bank debt (= one that you owe to a bank ) The company closed with bank debts of about £350 million.','the national debt (= the total amount that is owed by the government of a country ) Their national debt is the third largest in the world.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Braque acknowledged his debt to Impressionist painting.","translation":"براک به بدهی خود به نقاشی امپرسیونیستی اعتراف کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835033.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6ebf5729-3435-5b51-83a7-fa6cec8605b8','1382e53d-98bd-5eca-b5b3-c5938b8a6966',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'debt of gratitude/thanks','بدهی، دین؛ طلب (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have debts Fortunately, I have no debts.','run up debts ( also amass debts formal ) (= borrow more and more money ) At that time he was drinking a lot and running up debts.','pay off a debt (= pay the money back ) The first thing I''m going to do is pay off my debts.','repay/settle a debt formal (= pay the money back ) He was hoping he would soon have enough money to settle his debts.','clear your debts (= repay all of them ) It took him three years to clear his bank debts.','service a debt (= pay the interest on a debt, but not pay it back ) By then, she was borrowing more money just to service her debts.','write off/cancel a debt (= say officially that it does not have to be paid ) The bank finally agreed to write off the debt.','be burdened with/saddled with debts (= have big debts ) Many poor countries are saddled with huge debts.','reduce a debt The programme aims to reduce the debt of the world''s poorest countries.','big/large The debts got bigger and bigger.','huge (= very big ) Young people often leave university with huge debts.','unpaid/outstanding (= not yet paid ) The average outstanding debt on credit cards in Britain is now over £3,000.','heavy debts (= big debts ) The company wanted to reduce its heavy debts.','a bad debt (= one that is unlikely to be paid back ) Companies lose millions of pounds each year from having to write off bad debts.','a bank debt (= one that you owe to a bank ) The company closed with bank debts of about £350 million.','the national debt (= the total amount that is owed by the government of a country ) Their national debt is the third largest in the world.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('084eb956-2117-53e7-aada-dab589139575','8d504d62-c524-5266-a4e0-0d8531b88342',1,'going far down','خیلی پایین رفتن','spoken & written','going far down from the top or from the surface',null,'knee-deep','عمیق، ژرف؛ پرمخاطره (خواب)؛ آگاه (نظر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The castle is on an island surrounded by a deep lake.","translation":"این قلعه در جزیره ای است که توسط یک دریاچه عمیق احاطه شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001132759.mp3"},{"sentence":"The swimming pool has a deep end and a shallow end for kids.","translation":"این استخر دارای انتهایی عمیق و انتهایی کم عمق برای کودکان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706627.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’ll take the boat out into deep water where we can dive.","translation":"ما قایق را به داخل آب عمیق می بریم تا بتوانیم غواصی کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706628.mp3"},{"sentence":"a deep narrow valley","translation":"یک دره باریک عمیق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706632.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dig a hole around 12 inches deep.","translation":"حفره ای به عمق 12 اینچ حفر کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706635.mp3"},{"sentence":"In places, the snow was waist-deep (= deep enough to reach a person’s waist ) .","translation":"در جاهایی برف تا کمر بود (= به اندازه ای عمیق که به کمر آدم برسد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706638.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('84efdfcb-e5ab-5fd0-8c54-fec161c56f00','8d504d62-c524-5266-a4e0-0d8531b88342',2,'going far in','دور رفتن','spoken & written','going far in from the outside or from the front edge of something',null,null,'از بیرون یا از لبه جلویی چیزی به داخل می رود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a deep wound","translation":"یک زخم عمیق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001132774.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was sitting in a deep leather chair.","translation":"روی یک صندلی چرمی عمیق نشسته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706646.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
