('4057ad61-4df5-5a60-b32a-b27daf4e3555','841b4a7c-91e3-5c76-bd6a-b011339cba84',1,null,null,'spoken & written','diet drinks or foods contain less sugar or fat than ordinary ones',null,null,'نوشیدنی ها یا غذاهای رژیمی حاوی قند یا چربی کمتری نسبت به انواع معمولی هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a diet soda","translation":"یک نوشابه رژیمی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002084500.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4c42d531-c928-5b55-9861-a2fd5472aa75','46fe57b0-6a50-5711-8de3-ebc2aea2f9f3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','any substance that makes things dirty , such as mud or dust',null,null,'خاک، کثیفی، چرک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['remove the dirt (from something) First, remove any dirt from the cut.','brush off/wash off/clean off the dirt Wash the dirt off those boots before you come in.','something shows the dirt (= something looks dirty – used about colours ) Light-coloured clothes show the dirt rather quickly.','loose dirt (= that you can brush off easily ) Keep your pack clean by brushing off any loose dirt after use.','ingrained dirt (= under the surface of something and difficult to clean off ) We had to wash the walls to remove the ingrained dirt.','ground-in dirt (= difficult to remove because people have walked over something ) He had a lot of trouble getting rid of the ground-in dirt from the carpet.','be covered with dirt The kitchen floor was covered with dirt.','be black with dirt (= be very dirty ) Jack came in from the garden, his hands black with dirt.','a speck of dirt (= a very small piece of dirt ) Their house was so clean – there wasn’t a speck of dirt anywhere.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You should have seen the dirt on that car!","translation":"باید خاک آن ماشین را می دیدی!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001145679.mp3"},{"sentence":"His face and hands were black with dirt.","translation":"صورت و دستانش از خاک سیاه شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001695025.mp3"},{"sentence":"a patch of grass, covered in dog dirt (= waste from a dog’s bowels )","translation":"یک تکه علف، پوشیده از خاک سگ (= فضولات از روده سگ)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001695026.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4744aac2-b176-57e3-91a2-86a0aad80ce6','46fe57b0-6a50-5711-8de3-ebc2aea2f9f3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','earth or soil',null,null,'زمین یا خاک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['remove the dirt (from something) First, remove any dirt from the cut.','brush off/wash off/clean off the dirt Wash the dirt off those boots before you come in.','something shows the dirt (= something looks dirty – used about colours ) Light-coloured clothes show the dirt rather quickly.','loose dirt (= that you can brush off easily ) Keep your pack clean by brushing off any loose dirt after use.','ingrained dirt (= under the surface of something and difficult to clean off ) We had to wash the walls to remove the ingrained dirt.','ground-in dirt (= difficult to remove because people have walked over something ) He had a lot of trouble getting rid of the ground-in dirt from the carpet.','be covered with dirt The kitchen floor was covered with dirt.','be black with dirt (= be very dirty ) Jack came in from the garden, his hands black with dirt.','a speck of dirt (= a very small piece of dirt ) Their house was so clean – there wasn’t a speck of dirt anywhere.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Michael threw his handful of dirt onto the coffin.","translation":"مایکل مشتی خاکش را روی تابوت انداخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001145690.mp3"},{"sentence":"The children had been sitting in the dirt.","translation":"بچه ها توی خاک نشسته بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001695031.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('bea465dd-bf12-5247-9c84-894acdd3fc4a','46fe57b0-6a50-5711-8de3-ebc2aea2f9f3',3,null,null,'informal','information about someone’s private life or activities which could give people a bad opinion of them if it became known',null,null,'اطلاعاتی در مورد زندگی شخصی یا فعالیت‌های شخصی که در صورت معلوم شدن می‌تواند نظر بدی در مورد آنها ایجاد کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['remove the dirt (from something) First, remove any dirt from the cut.','brush off/wash off/clean off the dirt Wash the dirt off those boots before you come in.','something shows the dirt (= something looks dirty – used about colours ) Light-coloured clothes show the dirt rather quickly.','loose dirt (= that you can brush off easily ) Keep your pack clean by brushing off any loose dirt after use.','ingrained dirt (= under the surface of something and difficult to clean off ) We had to wash the walls to remove the ingrained dirt.','ground-in dirt (= difficult to remove because people have walked over something ) He had a lot of trouble getting rid of the ground-in dirt from the carpet.','be covered with dirt The kitchen floor was covered with dirt.','be black with dirt (= be very dirty ) Jack came in from the garden, his hands black with dirt.','a speck of dirt (= a very small piece of dirt ) Their house was so clean – there wasn’t a speck of dirt anywhere.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The newspapers had been digging up dirt on the president.","translation":"روزنامه ها روی رئیس جمهور خاک می زدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001695032.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0b01953d-963a-5629-9ef5-e72025e2780f','46fe57b0-6a50-5711-8de3-ebc2aea2f9f3',4,null,null,'spoken & written','talk, writing, a film etc that is considered bad or immoral because it is about sex',null,null,'صحبت کردن، نوشتن، فیلم و غیره که بد یا غیراخلاقی تلقی می شود زیرا در مورد رابطه جنسی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['remove the dirt (from something) First, remove any dirt from the cut.','brush off/wash off/clean off the dirt Wash the dirt off those boots before you come in.','something shows the dirt (= something looks dirty – used about colours ) Light-coloured clothes show the dirt rather quickly.','loose dirt (= that you can brush off easily ) Keep your pack clean by brushing off any loose dirt after use.','ingrained dirt (= under the surface of something and difficult to clean off ) We had to wash the walls to remove the ingrained dirt.','ground-in dirt (= difficult to remove because people have walked over something ) He had a lot of trouble getting rid of the ground-in dirt from the carpet.','be covered with dirt The kitchen floor was covered with dirt.','be black with dirt (= be very dirty ) Jack came in from the garden, his hands black with dirt.','a speck of dirt (= a very small piece of dirt ) Their house was so clean – there wasn’t a speck of dirt anywhere.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
