('94e8a207-1873-5e7f-91cf-9e3c4f75a1fa','86fb08b2-1d15-5903-8e2d-7095bb222da8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is very bad or harmful','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که بسیار بد یا مضر است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a great/greater evil He saw fascism as the greatest evil of his times.','a lesser evil (= a bad thing, but not as bad as something else ) She knew that she couldn''t leave the children, so she opted for the lesser evil and stayed.','a necessary evil (= something that is bad but necessary ) Most businesses see government regulation as a necessary evil.','a social evil (= something bad that happens in human society ) The community is being torn apart by poverty, drug abuse and other social evils.','a moral evil (= a bad thing in relation to principles of what is right and wrong ) Mental or physical torture is a moral evil, and it can never be justified.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She wanted to protect her children from the evils of the outside world.","translation":"او می خواست از فرزندانش در برابر بدی های دنیای بیرون محافظت کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643253.mp3"},{"sentence":"Poverty is one of the greatest social evils of our time.","translation":"فقر یکی از بزرگترین آسیب های اجتماعی عصر ماست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643254.mp3"},{"sentence":"the evils of capitalism","translation":"شرارت های سرمایه داری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223962.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('63483b4b-de90-5545-9321-88340d30a926','86fb08b2-1d15-5903-8e2d-7095bb222da8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','cruel or morally bad behaviour in general','[ uncountable ]',null,'به طور کلی رفتار ظالمانه یا اخلاقا بد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is too much evil in the world.","translation":"شر در دنیا خیلی زیاد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643255.mp3"},{"sentence":"the eternal struggle between good and evil","translation":"مبارزه ابدی بین خیر و شر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223967.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ceecccb5-9f79-5480-bbc4-d21a6262e785','10ed4647-a385-5573-a837-dfb7ebf06180',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a spoken or written test of knowledge , especially an important one',null,null,'امتحان، آزمون','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['take/do an exam ( also sit an exam British English ) We have to take exams at the end of each year.','pass an exam (= succeed in it ) Did you pass your final exam?','fail an exam If you fail the exam, you can retake it.','do well/badly in an exam British English , do well/badly on an exam American English: Maria always did well in her exams at school.','study for an exam ( also revise for an exam British English ) She has to study for her exams.','sail though an exam (= pass it easily ) Don’t worry - I’m sure you’ll sail through all your exams.','scrape through an exam (= only just pass it ) He managed to scrape through the exam and stay on the course.','flunk an exam American English informal (= fail it ) I flunked all my first year exams.','cheat in an exam British English , cheat on an exam American English: She was caught cheating in the exam.','retake an exam ( also resit an exam British English ) (= take it again because you did not do well the first time ) If you don’t do well, you’ll have to resit the exam in January.','a chemistry/French etc exam I knew I wouldn’t pass the German exam.','a written exam There is a written exam at the end of the course.','an oral exam (= in which you answer questions by speaking ) I have my French oral exams next week.','a mock exam British English (= one that you do to practise for the real exams ) He did well in the mock exams.','a practical exam (= in which you have to make or do things ) There’s a practical exam as well as a written one.','a final exam (= at the end of a course ) The students take their final exams in June.','the end of year/term exam British English: I knew I had to do well in the end of year exams.','high school exams Greg got good grades in all of his high school exams.','an entrance exam (= in order to enter a school or university ) Jane passed the entrance exam but decided not to go.','a professional exam (= to qualify in a profession, for example to be an accountant ) Once you’ve passed your professional exams, you can start to build up your experience.','the bar exam (= in order to become a lawyer ) He is studying for the bar exam.','board exams American English (= in order to become a nurse or doctor ) He failed his board exams in psychiatry.','exam results The school achieves consistently good exam results.','an exam paper I’ve still got dozens of exam papers to mark.','an exam question Read the exam questions carefully before writing your answers.','exam revision British English: I have to do my exam revision this weekend.','exam practice Schools say they have to spend too much time doing exam practice.','an exam essay/script (= that someone has written during an exam ) I’ve brought in some old exam scripts for us to look at.','exam technique (= good ways to succeed in exams ) Mr Frasier gave us some useful tips on exam technique.','exam marks Pupils were divided into classes with a similar range of ability, based on their previous exam marks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"At the end of each level, there’s an exam.","translation":"در پایان هر سطح، یک امتحان وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000534.mp3"},{"sentence":"How did you do in your exams ?","translation":"در امتحاناتت چطور بودی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001224404.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6b3f6d6c-f47a-531e-b58b-6cd790f5fa57','10ed4647-a385-5573-a837-dfb7ebf06180',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the paper on which the questions for an exam are written',null,null,'مقاله ای که سوالات امتحانی روی آن نوشته شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['take/do an exam ( also sit an exam British English ) We have to take exams at the end of each year.','pass an exam (= succeed in it ) Did you pass your final exam?','fail an exam If you fail the exam, you can retake it.','do well/badly in an exam British English , do well/badly on an exam American English: Maria always did well in her exams at school.','study for an exam ( also revise for an exam British English ) She has to study for her exams.','sail though an exam (= pass it easily ) Don’t worry - I’m sure you’ll sail through all your exams.','scrape through an exam (= only just pass it ) He managed to scrape through the exam and stay on the course.','flunk an exam American English informal (= fail it ) I flunked all my first year exams.','cheat in an exam British English , cheat on an exam American English: She was caught cheating in the exam.','retake an exam ( also resit an exam British English ) (= take it again because you did not do well the first time ) If you don’t do well, you’ll have to resit the exam in January.','a chemistry/French etc exam I knew I wouldn’t pass the German exam.','a written exam There is a written exam at the end of the course.','an oral exam (= in which you answer questions by speaking ) I have my French oral exams next week.','a mock exam British English (= one that you do to practise for the real exams ) He did well in the mock exams.','a practical exam (= in which you have to make or do things ) There’s a practical exam as well as a written one.','a final exam (= at the end of a course ) The students take their final exams in June.','the end of year/term exam British English: I knew I had to do well in the end of year exams.','high school exams Greg got good grades in all of his high school exams.','an entrance exam (= in order to enter a school or university ) Jane passed the entrance exam but decided not to go.','a professional exam (= to qualify in a profession, for example to be an accountant ) Once you’ve passed your professional exams, you can start to build up your experience.','the bar exam (= in order to become a lawyer ) He is studying for the bar exam.','board exams American English (= in order to become a nurse or doctor ) He failed his board exams in psychiatry.','exam results The school achieves consistently good exam results.','an exam paper I’ve still got dozens of exam papers to mark.','an exam question Read the exam questions carefully before writing your answers.','exam revision British English: I have to do my exam revision this weekend.','exam practice Schools say they have to spend too much time doing exam practice.','an exam essay/script (= that someone has written during an exam ) I’ve brought in some old exam scripts for us to look at.','exam technique (= good ways to succeed in exams ) Mr Frasier gave us some useful tips on exam technique.','exam marks Pupils were divided into classes with a similar range of ability, based on their previous exam marks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Do not open your exams until I tell you.","translation":"تا من بهت نگم امتحاناتو باز نکن.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001224425.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('68fa8c0d-1658-5b53-92b2-81842401d088','10ed4647-a385-5573-a837-dfb7ebf06180',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a set of medical tests',null,null,'مجموعه ای از آزمایشات پزشکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['take/do an exam ( also sit an exam British English ) We have to take exams at the end of each year.','pass an exam (= succeed in it ) Did you pass your final exam?','fail an exam If you fail the exam, you can retake it.','do well/badly in an exam British English , do well/badly on an exam American English: Maria always did well in her exams at school.','study for an exam ( also revise for an exam British English ) She has to study for her exams.','sail though an exam (= pass it easily ) Don’t worry - I’m sure you’ll sail through all your exams.','scrape through an exam (= only just pass it ) He managed to scrape through the exam and stay on the course.','flunk an exam American English informal (= fail it ) I flunked all my first year exams.','cheat in an exam British English , cheat on an exam American English: She was caught cheating in the exam.','retake an exam ( also resit an exam British English ) (= take it again because you did not do well the first time ) If you don’t do well, you’ll have to resit the exam in January.','a chemistry/French etc exam I knew I wouldn’t pass the German exam.','a written exam There is a written exam at the end of the course.','an oral exam (= in which you answer questions by speaking ) I have my French oral exams next week.','a mock exam British English (= one that you do to practise for the real exams ) He did well in the mock exams.','a practical exam (= in which you have to make or do things ) There’s a practical exam as well as a written one.','a final exam (= at the end of a course ) The students take their final exams in June.','the end of year/term exam British English: I knew I had to do well in the end of year exams.','high school exams Greg got good grades in all of his high school exams.','an entrance exam (= in order to enter a school or university ) Jane passed the entrance exam but decided not to go.','a professional exam (= to qualify in a profession, for example to be an accountant ) Once you’ve passed your professional exams, you can start to build up your experience.','the bar exam (= in order to become a lawyer ) He is studying for the bar exam.','board exams American English (= in order to become a nurse or doctor ) He failed his board exams in psychiatry.','exam results The school achieves consistently good exam results.','an exam paper I’ve still got dozens of exam papers to mark.','an exam question Read the exam questions carefully before writing your answers.','exam revision British English: I have to do my exam revision this weekend.','exam practice Schools say they have to spend too much time doing exam practice.','an exam essay/script (= that someone has written during an exam ) I’ve brought in some old exam scripts for us to look at.','exam technique (= good ways to succeed in exams ) Mr Frasier gave us some useful tips on exam technique.','exam marks Pupils were divided into classes with a similar range of ability, based on their previous exam marks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"an eye exam","translation":"یک معاینه چشم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001224420.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ddf0c903-87ba-5c77-b785-9ab2a1d3a55d','fb23a686-e15d-5c9e-98d9-65b6ac9f9162',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a door or space through which you can leave a public room, building etc',null,null,'خروجی، در خروج؛ خروج (برنامه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fire/emergency exit (= a special door, used if there is an emergency or a fire ) Fire crews discovered that the club’s fire exit door had been locked.','the front/rear/side exit When the lights dimmed, she slipped out by the rear exit.','the nearest exit Please leave the building in an orderly fashion, using the nearest exit.','head for/make for the exit (= go to the exit ) Disappointed fans began heading for the exits.','use an exit In the event of a fire, please use the emergency exit nearest to you.','an exit door Exit doors shouldn’t be blocked at any time.','an exit route (= a way out of a building, plane etc, used in an emergency or a fire ) Staff must become familiar with the building’s exit routes.','an exit sign (= one showing where an exit is ) There was a red glowing exit sign over the door.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We made for the nearest exit.","translation":"برای نزدیکترین خروجی حرکت کردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230707.mp3"},{"sentence":"an exit door","translation":"یک درب خروجی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230708.mp3"},{"sentence":"Two men were blocking her exit.","translation":"دو مرد جلوی خروج او را گرفته بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001611977.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('453b8c8b-ce7b-59e2-87c6-fb9cb19f9016','fb23a686-e15d-5c9e-98d9-65b6ac9f9162',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when you leave a room or building','[ usually singular ]',null,'وقتی از یک اتاق یا ساختمان خارج می شوید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"They made a quick exit when they saw the police approaching.","translation":"وقتی دیدند پلیس در حال نزدیک شدن است، سریع از آنجا خارج شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001611978.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2f9d128d-f14b-5e96-98ee-f3eaed6bbbd6','fb23a686-e15d-5c9e-98d9-65b6ac9f9162',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a place where vehicles can leave a road such as a motorway , and join another road',null,null,'مکانی که وسایل نقلیه می توانند جاده ای مانند بزرگراه را ترک کنند و به جاده دیگری بپیوندند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Take the next exit for Lynchburg.","translation":"از خروجی بعدی به سمت لینچبرگ بروید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230730.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('55353d52-6ab8-54ce-a1ae-c77ede7aef6f','fb23a686-e15d-5c9e-98d9-65b6ac9f9162',4,null,null,'spoken & written','when someone stops being involved in a competition or business, especially because they have not been successful','[ usually singular ]',null,'زمانی که شخصی دیگر در یک رقابت یا تجارت شرکت نمی کند، به خصوص به این دلیل که موفق نبوده است',array['departure']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"France’s early exit from the World Cup","translation":"خروج زودهنگام فرانسه از جام جهانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230735.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1d527a66-7be6-5cb5-8f51-87703b60c080','6ca3b941-f4f2-560d-9b52-b61b1e037e46',1,null,null,'formal','to leave a place',null,null,'برای ترک یک مکان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I exited through a side window.","translation":"از پنجره کناری خارج شدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230747.mp3"},{"sentence":"He exited the courtroom in a fury.","translation":"او با عصبانیت از دادگاه خارج شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001611990.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b1c4449e-6850-51ea-9697-b19ba67ea04d','6ca3b941-f4f2-560d-9b52-b61b1e037e46',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to stop using a computer program',null,null,'برای توقف استفاده از یک برنامه کامپیوتری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Press F3 to exit.","translation":"برای خروج F3 را فشار دهید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230757.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5e3135ff-f89c-5481-9ffd-2ed7ace85e1a','6ca3b941-f4f2-560d-9b52-b61b1e037e46',3,null,null,'spoken & written','used in the instructions of a play to tell an actor to leave the stage',null,null,'در دستورالعمل یک نمایشنامه استفاده می شود تا به بازیگر بگوید صحنه را ترک کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Exit Hamlet, bearing the body of Polonius.","translation":"از هملت با جسد پولونیوس خارج شوید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230763.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6cca50a3-bede-5367-9aaa-ecf27f7c1555','79676da2-222f-5250-9d6d-3617e2f2a1e9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a British organization which aims to change the law against helping seriously ill people to die if they wish to. The organization gives advice to such people and their families. The Hemlock Society is a similar organization in the US.',null,'euthanasia','یک سازمان بریتانیایی که قصد دارد قانون مبارزه با کمک به بیماران سخت را برای مرگ در صورت تمایل تغییر دهد. این سازمان به این افراد و خانواده هایشان توصیه هایی می کند. انجمن Hemlock یک سازمان مشابه در ایالات متحده است.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1abe9ad8-9022-5e9b-b07e-5a6c029edaa3','c4b9d77e-dd41-5f5a-a16b-c8d5fa68ff86',1,'front of your head','جلوی سرت','spoken & written','the front part of your head, where your eyes, nose , and mouth are',null,null,'صورت، چهره؛ ظاهر (بالاخره)؛ طرف (سطح)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pretty/beautiful/handsome etc Her face was beautiful in the morning light.','round/oval/square Her face was round and jolly.','thin/narrow Tears rolled down her thin face.','pale/dark His face suddenly became pale and I thought he was going to faint.','an angular face (= so thin that you can see the bones ) She stared at his dark, angular face.','sad/serious Maggie looked at him with a sad face.','happy/smiling Shelley looked at the children’s happy faces.','a grinning face He looked down at the boy’s grinning face.','angry Beth’s angry face stared fiercely at her husband.','worried/anxious My father watched us go with a worried face.','puzzled He looked at his son’s puzzled face.','blank/impassive (= showing no emotion or thoughts ) What was she really thinking behind that blank face?','wrinkled/lined (= with a lot of small lines, especially because of old age ) His wrinkled face must once have been handsome.','scowling (= showing that you are not pleased about something ) He looked around and saw his boss''s scowling face behind him.','a long face (= an unhappy expression ) What’s the long face for?','somebody’s face goes/turns red (= becomes red ) His face went red with embarrassment.','somebody’s face goes/turns pale (= becomes pale ) I saw her face go pale when he walked in.','somebody’s face lights up/brightens (= they start to look happy ) Denise’s face lit up when she heard the news.','somebody’s face darkens (= they start to look angry or threatening ) She handed him the letter and his face darkened.','somebody’s face falls (= they look sad or disappointed ) Her face fell when she saw who it was.','pull/make a face (= to change your expression to make people laugh or to show you are angry, disappointed etc ) Here’s a funny photo of Joe pulling a face.','somebody’s face is contorted with anger/rage (= someone’s face is twisted out of its normal shape because they are angry ) Eve’s face was contorted with anger as she picked up the broken vase.','a look/expression on somebody’s face She had a rather surprised look on her face. I could tell by the look on Dan’s face that he was disappointed.','a smile/grin/frown on somebody’s face There was a mischievous grin on her face. He was reading the newspaper with a frown on his face.','you can see something in somebody’s face (= you know what someone is feeling from the expression on their face ) She could see the despair in his face.','something is written all over somebody’s face (= their feelings can be seen very clearly in their expression ) You’re jealous – it’s written all over your face!','you should have seen somebody’s face (= used to say that someone was very angry, surprised etc ) You should have seen his face when I told him that I was resigning.','a face like thunder (= a very angry expression ) The boss had a face like thunder when he arrived this morning.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She had a beautiful face.","translation":"او چهره زیبایی داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204378.mp3"},{"sentence":"Her face was white with fear.","translation":"صورتش از ترس سفید شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001637988.mp3"},{"sentence":"A big smile spread across his face.","translation":"لبخند بزرگی روی صورتش پخش شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001637989.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt like punching him in the face.","translation":"دلم می خواست بکوبم تو صورتش.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001637991.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('0d27cc3b-314c-5374-97f8-976d3d029883','c4b9d77e-dd41-5f5a-a16b-c8d5fa68ff86',2,'expression','بیان','spoken & written','an expression on someone’s face',null,null,'بیان در صورت کسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pretty/beautiful/handsome etc Her face was beautiful in the morning light.','round/oval/square Her face was round and jolly.','thin/narrow Tears rolled down her thin face.','pale/dark His face suddenly became pale and I thought he was going to faint.','an angular face (= so thin that you can see the bones ) She stared at his dark, angular face.','sad/serious Maggie looked at him with a sad face.','happy/smiling Shelley looked at the children’s happy faces.','a grinning face He looked down at the boy’s grinning face.','angry Beth’s angry face stared fiercely at her husband.','worried/anxious My father watched us go with a worried face.','puzzled He looked at his son’s puzzled face.','blank/impassive (= showing no emotion or thoughts ) What was she really thinking behind that blank face?','wrinkled/lined (= with a lot of small lines, especially because of old age ) His wrinkled face must once have been handsome.','scowling (= showing that you are not pleased about something ) He looked around and saw his boss''s scowling face behind him.','a long face (= an unhappy expression ) What’s the long face for?','somebody’s face goes/turns red (= becomes red ) His face went red with embarrassment.','somebody’s face goes/turns pale (= becomes pale ) I saw her face go pale when he walked in.','somebody’s face lights up/brightens (= they start to look happy ) Denise’s face lit up when she heard the news.','somebody’s face darkens (= they start to look angry or threatening ) She handed him the letter and his face darkened.','somebody’s face falls (= they look sad or disappointed ) Her face fell when she saw who it was.','pull/make a face (= to change your expression to make people laugh or to show you are angry, disappointed etc ) Here’s a funny photo of Joe pulling a face.','somebody’s face is contorted with anger/rage (= someone’s face is twisted out of its normal shape because they are angry ) Eve’s face was contorted with anger as she picked up the broken vase.','a look/expression on somebody’s face She had a rather surprised look on her face. I could tell by the look on Dan’s face that he was disappointed.','a smile/grin/frown on somebody’s face There was a mischievous grin on her face. He was reading the newspaper with a frown on his face.','you can see something in somebody’s face (= you know what someone is feeling from the expression on their face ) She could see the despair in his face.','something is written all over somebody’s face (= their feelings can be seen very clearly in their expression ) You’re jealous – it’s written all over your face!','you should have seen somebody’s face (= used to say that someone was very angry, surprised etc ) You should have seen his face when I told him that I was resigning.','a face like thunder (= a very angry expression ) The boss had a face like thunder when he arrived this morning.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ll never forget my father’s face – I’d never seen him so upset before.","translation":"من هرگز چهره پدرم را فراموش نمی کنم - قبلاً هرگز او را اینقدر ناراحت ندیده بودم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001970091.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4fb62ac4-63bf-50b6-a965-a9bdd236babc','c4b9d77e-dd41-5f5a-a16b-c8d5fa68ff86',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'keep a straight face','صورت، چهره؛ ظاهر (بالاخره)؛ طرف (سطح)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
