('e93cea1d-fb8e-529b-abb7-e2358a253188','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',1,'difficult situation','وضعیت دشوار','spoken & written','if you face or are faced with a difficult situation, or if a difficult situation faces you, it is going to affect you and you must deal with it',null,null,'مواجه شدن، رویارویی؛ رو به رو بودن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Emergency services are facing additional problems this winter.","translation":"خدمات اورژانس در زمستان امسال با مشکلات بیشتری مواجه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001823742.mp3"},{"sentence":"The president faces the difficult task of putting the economy back on its feet.","translation":"رئیس جمهور با کار دشواری مواجه است که اقتصاد را دوباره روی پای خود بازگرداند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204684.mp3"},{"sentence":"McManus is facing the biggest challenge of his career.","translation":"مک مانوس با بزرگترین چالش دوران حرفه ای خود روبرو است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638129.mp3"},{"sentence":"As the project comes to an end, many workers now face an uncertain future .","translation":"با پایان یافتن پروژه، بسیاری از کارگران اکنون با آینده نامعلومی روبرو هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638130.mp3"},{"sentence":"He must face the prospect of financial ruin.","translation":"او باید با چشم انداز نابودی مالی روبرو شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001823763.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was faced with the awful job of breaking the news to the girl’s family.","translation":"من با کار افتضاحی مواجه شدم که خبر را به خانواده دختر بدهم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204688.mp3"},{"sentence":"the difficulties faced by the police","translation":"مشکلات پیش روی پلیس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638131.mp3"},{"sentence":"If he is found guilty, he faces up to 12 years in jail.","translation":"اگر مجرم شناخته شود، با 12 سال زندان مواجه خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638133.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was the first member of the former government to face criminal charges.","translation":"او اولین عضو دولت سابق بود که با اتهامات جنایی روبرو شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638137.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('f78918cd-c0ae-5ef2-b1af-77b052851f10','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',2,'admit a problem exists','اعتراف کنید که مشکلی وجود دارد','spoken & written','to accept that a difficult situation or problem exists, even though you would prefer to ignore it',null,null,'بپذیرید که یک موقعیت یا مشکل وجود دارد، حتی اگر ترجیح می دهید آن را نادیده بگیرید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Many couples refuse to face the fact that there are problems in their marriage.","translation":"بسیاری از زوج ها از رویارویی با این واقعیت که در زندگی مشترکشان مشکلاتی وجود دارد، امتناع می ورزند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204695.mp3"},{"sentence":"You’ve got to face facts , Rachel. You can’t survive on a salary that low.","translation":"باید با حقایق روبرو شوی، راشل. شما نمی توانید با حقوقی به این کم دوام بیاورید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638142.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had to face the awful truth that she no longer loved him.","translation":"او باید با این حقیقت وحشتناک روبرو می شد که او دیگر او را دوست ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204701.mp3"},{"sentence":"Face it, kid. You’re never going to be a rock star.","translation":"با آن روبرو شو، بچه شما هرگز یک ستاره راک نخواهید بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638153.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('17d7bbcf-2eb0-55a4-a736-c8b217f25d19','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'can’t face','مواجه شدن، رویارویی؛ رو به رو بودن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e980da57-8c5d-551d-b5a7-131e9ac2dcec','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',4,'talk/deal with somebody','صحبت کردن / معامله با کسی','spoken & written','to talk or deal with someone, when this is unpleasant or difficult for you',null,null,'صحبت کردن یا معامله با کسی، زمانی که این برای شما ناخوشایند یا دشوار است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’re going to have to face him sooner or later.","translation":"دیر یا زود باید با او روبرو شوید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204749.mp3"},{"sentence":"I don’t know how I’m going to face her after what happened.","translation":"نمی دانم بعد از این اتفاق چگونه با او روبرو خواهم شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638170.mp3"},{"sentence":"The accident left her feeling depressed and unable to face the world (= be with people and live a normal life ) .","translation":"این حادثه باعث شد که او احساس افسردگی کند و قادر به رویارویی با دنیا نباشد (= با مردم باشد و یک زندگی عادی داشته باشد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638171.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('29b4d8a3-0eb1-518e-9728-78711f65f259','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',5,'be opposite','مقابل باشد','spoken & written','to be opposite someone or something, or to be looking or pointing in a particular direction',null,null,'روبروی کسی یا چیزی بودن، یا به سمتی خاص نگاه کردن یا اشاره کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The two men stood facing each other, smiling.","translation":"دو مرد روبروی هم ایستاده بودند و لبخند می زدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204719.mp3"},{"sentence":"When he turned to face her, he seemed annoyed.","translation":"وقتی به سمت او برگشت، به نظر آزرده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638176.mp3"},{"sentence":"Lunch is served on the terrace facing the sea.","translation":"ناهار در تراس رو به دریا سرو می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204720.mp3"},{"sentence":"a south-facing garden","translation":"باغی رو به جنوب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001823433.mp3"},{"sentence":"The dining room faces east.","translation":"اتاق غذاخوری رو به شرق است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204724.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('5e51130a-84dc-5a76-b630-c606b56ef998','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',6,'opponent/team','حریف/تیم','spoken & written','to play against an opponent or team in a game or competition',null,null,'برای بازی در برابر حریف یا تیم در یک بازی یا مسابقه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Martinez will face Robertson in tomorrow’s final.","translation":"مارتینز در فینال فردا به مصاف رابرتسون خواهد رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001204744.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('37c98d44-2fe1-5200-8359-a627d20c779f','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'face the music','مواجه شدن، رویارویی؛ رو به رو بودن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d2cbcc8d-3131-5f17-a3d8-2dc7b75801f6','fc8de14a-c787-5c6d-a29b-f63d47466aa0',8,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be faced with stone/concrete etc','مواجه شدن، رویارویی؛ رو به رو بودن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['face a problem She told me about some of the problems she was facing.','face a difficulty The hotel’s owners were facing financial difficulties.','face a challenge The coal industry faces serious challenges.','face the task of doing something He faced the task of preparing a three-course meal for 50 people.','face a danger He has the courage to face danger in spite of fear.','face opposition (= deal with strong disagreement ) The government faced opposition from the Liberal Democrats.','face charges (= be accused of a crime and have to go to a court of law ) He faces charges of fraud and theft.','face an uncertain/difficult future The company is facing an uncertain future.','face the prospect of something (= something in the future is going to affect you and you will have to deal with it ) Many coastal cities face the prospect of disastrous flooding.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('559f794c-b1a5-57d5-8dec-46570211580d','78e6ed5a-994c-5f2a-a81b-44dbeb04fc40',1,'true information','اطلاعات واقعی','spoken & written','a piece of information that is known to be true','[ countable ]',null,'واقعیت، حقیقت؛ حقیقت (درست)؛ فعل و مضرب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the basic/key facts The report outlines the basic facts concerning the case.','a well-known fact It is a well-known fact that new cars lose a lot of their value in the first year.','a little-known fact It is a little-known fact that the actor was born in London.','an interesting fact The research revealed some interesting facts about the behaviour of cats.','a curious/remarkable fact It is a remarkable fact that elephants do not use their trunks to suck up water until they are over four months old.','hard facts (= information that is definitely true and can be proven ) His theory is supported by hard facts.','a historical/scientific fact This was presented as a historical fact when it was just an opinion.','the bare facts (= only the basic general facts of a situation ) We know the bare facts of his life, but nothing about what he was really like.','give somebody/provide the facts Newspapers have a duty to give their readers the facts.','establish/piece together the facts (= find out what actually happened in a situation ) The police are still piecing together the facts.','examine the facts I decided to examine the facts for myself.','state the facts (= say what you know is true ) Press reports often fail to state the facts completely.','stick to the facts (= say only what you know is true ) Just stick to the facts when the police interview you.','know for a fact (= used to say that something is definitely true ) I know for a fact that she is older than me.','get your facts right/straight (= make sure that what you say or believe is correct ) You should get your facts straight before making accusations.','get your facts wrong It’s no use putting together a beautifully-written argument if you get your facts wrong.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The book is full of facts about the World Cup.","translation":"کتاب پر از حقایق در مورد جام جهانی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000551.mp3"},{"sentence":"First of all, we need to know the facts of the case.","translation":"اول از همه، ما باید واقعیت های پرونده را بدانیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000552.mp3"},{"sentence":"The divorce rate is twice as high as in the 1950s – that’s a fact.","translation":"نرخ طلاق دو برابر بیشتر از دهه 1950 است - این یک واقعیت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206571.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘She used to be a professional singer.’ ‘Is that a fact?’","translation":"\"او قبلا یک خواننده حرفه ای بود.\" \"این یک واقعیت است؟\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638249.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('42ba9d50-52a6-5df2-a585-0e03bb2da453','78e6ed5a-994c-5f2a-a81b-44dbeb04fc40',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the fact (that)','واقعیت، حقیقت؛ حقیقت (درست)؛ فعل و مضرب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the basic/key facts The report outlines the basic facts concerning the case.','a well-known fact It is a well-known fact that new cars lose a lot of their value in the first year.','a little-known fact It is a little-known fact that the actor was born in London.','an interesting fact The research revealed some interesting facts about the behaviour of cats.','a curious/remarkable fact It is a remarkable fact that elephants do not use their trunks to suck up water until they are over four months old.','hard facts (= information that is definitely true and can be proven ) His theory is supported by hard facts.','a historical/scientific fact This was presented as a historical fact when it was just an opinion.','the bare facts (= only the basic general facts of a situation ) We know the bare facts of his life, but nothing about what he was really like.','give somebody/provide the facts Newspapers have a duty to give their readers the facts.','establish/piece together the facts (= find out what actually happened in a situation ) The police are still piecing together the facts.','examine the facts I decided to examine the facts for myself.','state the facts (= say what you know is true ) Press reports often fail to state the facts completely.','stick to the facts (= say only what you know is true ) Just stick to the facts when the police interview you.','know for a fact (= used to say that something is definitely true ) I know for a fact that she is older than me.','get your facts right/straight (= make sure that what you say or believe is correct ) You should get your facts straight before making accusations.','get your facts wrong It’s no use putting together a beautifully-written argument if you get your facts wrong.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
