('8a9ad0de-9b18-5f67-90b4-d0af92077b91','bee47c64-8d23-5974-ae8a-4ed189242a4f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to worry a lot about things that may not be very important',null,null,'نگرانی زیادی در مورد چیزهایی که ممکن است خیلی مهم نباشند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I wish you’d stop fussing – I’ll be perfectly all right.","translation":"کاش دست از سر و صدا کردن بردارید - من کاملاً خوب خواهم شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001317100.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cb959e44-f3dd-5c5c-aee9-1e3f484243cf','bee47c64-8d23-5974-ae8a-4ed189242a4f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to pay too much attention to small unimportant details',null,null,'توجه بیش از حد به جزئیات کوچک و بی اهمیت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Paul was fussing with his clothes, trying to get his tie straight.","translation":"پل با لباس هایش قاطی می کرد و سعی می کرد کراواتش را صاف کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001317107.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('215271b9-f9e5-5c79-be41-6cfc5255543d','bee47c64-8d23-5974-ae8a-4ed189242a4f',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to behave in an unhappy or angry way',null,null,'رفتار ناراضی یا عصبانی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The baby woke up and started to fuss.","translation":"بچه از خواب بیدار شد و شروع به داد و بیداد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001317120.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9cc9e769-341e-5845-848f-668859073842','9bcb7508-8e40-555e-be23-4683c408199a',1,'get something','چیزی بگیر','spoken & written','to obtain or achieve something you want or need','[ transitive ]',null,'به دست آوردن؛ کسب کردن؛ افزایش یافتن (وزن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['gain control The government of mainland China gained control of the island in 1683.','gain power Many women wanted to gain power in a male-dominated world.','gain independence Jamaica has had this flag since 1962, when it gained independence from Britain.','gain a reputation He had gained a reputation as a crook.','gain notoriety (= become famous, especially for doing something bad ) He gained notoriety as the author of a controversial novel.','gain support The proposal failed to gain support.','gain popularity Governments gain popularity by cutting taxes.','gain acceptance The theory has gradually gained acceptance among scientists.','gain credibility (= start to be believed or trusted, or start to be thought of as good ) Screen actors feel that they gain credibility when they perform on stage.','gain experience In her first job, she gained experience as a programme manager.','gain knowledge Knowledge gained from the research will be used directly to help patients.','gain confidence The managers were gaining confidence in their ability to take calculated risks.','gain strength He is beginning to gain strength again after his illness.','gain an understanding (= get knowledge based on learning and experience ) Drama is one of the key ways in which children can gain an understanding of themselves and of others.','gain an insight (into something) (= get a chance to understand more about something ) You can gain an insight into horses’ feelings by the physical signs they give out.','gain momentum (= keep increasing ) In the 1850s and 1860s, the British colonisation of India gained momentum.','quickly/rapidly gain something Adam quickly gained the respect of the soldiers under his command.','steadily gain something The king was steadily gaining more support.','gradually gain something He is gradually gaining confidence in his own abilities.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Radical left-wing parties gained control of local authorities.","translation":"احزاب چپ رادیکال کنترل مقامات محلی را به دست گرفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001318175.mp3"},{"sentence":"After gaining independence in 1957, it was renamed ‘Ghana’.","translation":"پس از به دست آوردن استقلال در سال 1957، نام آن به \"غنا\" تغییر یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001318174.mp3"},{"sentence":"He gained a doctorate in Chemical Engineering.","translation":"وی مدرک دکتری خود را در رشته مهندسی شیمی دریافت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001697657.mp3"},{"sentence":"She got a degree in English.","translation":"او مدرک زبان انگلیسی گرفت.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,4),
('f300cadf-f738-5385-9e2e-4d4c87ed2d68','9bcb7508-8e40-555e-be23-4683c408199a',2,'get gradually','به تدریج دریافت کنید','spoken & written','to gradually get more and more of a quality, feeling etc, especially a useful or valuable one','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'به تدریج کیفیت، احساس و غیره بیشتر و بیشتر به دست آورید، مخصوصاً یک کیفیت مفید یا ارزشمند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['gain control The government of mainland China gained control of the island in 1683.','gain power Many women wanted to gain power in a male-dominated world.','gain independence Jamaica has had this flag since 1962, when it gained independence from Britain.','gain a reputation He had gained a reputation as a crook.','gain notoriety (= become famous, especially for doing something bad ) He gained notoriety as the author of a controversial novel.','gain support The proposal failed to gain support.','gain popularity Governments gain popularity by cutting taxes.','gain acceptance The theory has gradually gained acceptance among scientists.','gain credibility (= start to be believed or trusted, or start to be thought of as good ) Screen actors feel that they gain credibility when they perform on stage.','gain experience In her first job, she gained experience as a programme manager.','gain knowledge Knowledge gained from the research will be used directly to help patients.','gain confidence The managers were gaining confidence in their ability to take calculated risks.','gain strength He is beginning to gain strength again after his illness.','gain an understanding (= get knowledge based on learning and experience ) Drama is one of the key ways in which children can gain an understanding of themselves and of others.','gain an insight (into something) (= get a chance to understand more about something ) You can gain an insight into horses’ feelings by the physical signs they give out.','gain momentum (= keep increasing ) In the 1850s and 1860s, the British colonisation of India gained momentum.','quickly/rapidly gain something Adam quickly gained the respect of the soldiers under his command.','steadily gain something The king was steadily gaining more support.','gradually gain something He is gradually gaining confidence in his own abilities.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She has gained a reputation as a good communicator.","translation":"او به عنوان یک ارتباط خوب شهرت پیدا کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001697658.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many of his ideas have gained popular support .","translation":"بسیاری از ایده های او مورد حمایت مردمی قرار گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001697662.mp3"},{"sentence":"an opportunity to gain experience in a work environment","translation":"فرصتی برای کسب تجربه در یک محیط کاری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001697668.mp3"},{"sentence":"The youngsters gradually gain confidence in their abilities.","translation":"جوانان به تدریج به توانایی های خود اعتماد می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001697672.mp3"},{"sentence":"The sport has gained in popularity in recent years.","translation":"این ورزش در سال های اخیر محبوبیت زیادی پیدا کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001782825.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('9957820d-6a1e-5a0b-a92c-f08ad60230cc','9bcb7508-8e40-555e-be23-4683c408199a',3,'advantage','مزیت','spoken & written','to get an advantage from a situation, opportunity, or event','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای کسب مزیت از یک موقعیت، فرصت یا رویداد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is much to be gained from seeking expert advice early.","translation":"با جستجوی زودهنگام مشاوره متخصص می توان چیزهای زیادی به دست آورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001318201.mp3"},{"sentence":"an attempt to gain a competitive advantage over their rivals","translation":"تلاش برای کسب مزیت رقابتی نسبت به رقبای خود","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001697678.mp3"},{"sentence":"Who really stands to gain (= is likely to get an advantage ) from these tax cuts?","translation":"چه کسی واقعاً از این کاهش مالیات سود می برد (= احتمالاً مزیتی کسب خواهد کرد؟)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001318205.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s nothing to be gained (= it will not help you ) by losing your temper.","translation":"با از دست دادن عصبانیت چیزی به دست نمی آید (= به شما کمک نمی کند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001318209.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
