is hair.','run your fingers through somebody’s hair (= touch someone’s hair in a loving way ) He ran his fingers through her smooth silky hair.','ruffle somebody’s hair (= rub it in a kind friendly way ) He patted me on the back and ruffled my hair.','hair loss The drug can cause hair loss.','hair colour British English , hair color American English Genes control characteristics such as hair colour and eye colour.','hair dye The survey showed that 75% of women have used hair dye.','a strand/wisp of hair (= a thin piece of hair ) She brushed away a strand of hair from her eyes.','a lock of hair (= a fairly thick piece of hair ) She tossed a stray lock of hair back off her forehead.','a mop of hair (= a large amount of thick untidy hair ) He had an unruly mop of brown hair.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
