('fe0bcb97-980d-5546-89c9-dd61cffe66c8','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if you have to do something, you must do it because it is necessary or because someone makes you do it',null,null,'(فعل کمکی) باید (have to: ناگزیر بودن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We don’t have to rush – there’s plenty of time.","translation":"ما نیازی به عجله نداریم - زمان زیادی وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526033.mp3"},{"sentence":"I hate having to get up early in the morning.","translation":"از صبح زود بیدار شدن متنفرم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526034.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you earn more than £5,000, you will have to pay tax.","translation":"اگر بیش از 5000 پوند درآمد داشته باشید، باید مالیات بپردازید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526035.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ve got to be at the hospital at 4 o''clock.","translation":"من باید ساعت 4 در بیمارستان باشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001786946.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’ll have to be on a Sunday. I’ll be working every other day.","translation":"باید یکشنبه باشد. من یک روز در میان کار خواهم کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001786947.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('a77cee2d-b237-510e-b2bf-006e7efd26bc','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used to say that it is important that something happens, or that something must happen if something else is to happen',null,null,'می گفت مهم است که اتفاقی بیفتد یا اگر قرار است اتفاق دیگری بیفتد باید اتفاقی بیفتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There has to be an end to the violence.","translation":"باید به خشونت پایان داده شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526039.mp3"},{"sentence":"You’ve got to believe me!","translation":"تو باید منو باور کنی!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526040.mp3"},{"sentence":"There will have to be a complete ceasefire before the Government will agree to talks.","translation":"قبل از موافقت دولت با مذاکرات، باید آتش بس کامل برقرار شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526041.mp3"},{"sentence":"You have to be good to succeed in this game.","translation":"برای موفقیت در این بازی باید خوب باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001786948.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('c57062a8-64ac-5d15-a690-61bc7965e717','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',3,null,null,'spoken & written','used to tell someone how to do something',null,null,'به کسی می گفت که چگونه کاری را انجام دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"First of all you have to mix the flour and the butter.","translation":"اول از همه باید آرد و کره را با هم مخلوط کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526045.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0dd207a6-81ed-5e6f-8a72-9693c5ad55a6','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',4,null,null,'spoken & written','used to say that you are sure that something will happen or something is true',null,null,'می گفت مطمئن هستید که اتفاقی می افتد یا چیزی درست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"House prices have to go up sooner or later.","translation":"قیمت خانه ها دیر یا زود باید افزایش یابد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526049.mp3"},{"sentence":"This has to be a mistake.","translation":"این باید یک اشتباه باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001786949.mp3"},{"sentence":"You have got to be joking!","translation":"باید شوخی کنی!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001786950.mp3"},{"sentence":"No one else could have done it – it had to be Neville.","translation":"هیچ کس دیگری نمی توانست این کار را انجام دهد - باید نویل بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526050.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('7249a103-cae4-5a49-a20f-de4dbc414a0f','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',5,null,null,'spoken & written','used to suggest that someone should do something because you think it would be enjoyable or useful',null,null,'به این پیشنهاد می‌شد که کسی باید کاری را انجام دهد، زیرا فکر می‌کنید لذت‌بخش یا مفید است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’ll have to come and meet my wife some time.","translation":"شما باید بیایید و همسرم را ملاقات کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001786954.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b503a755-1a5d-55f7-b3c5-999bd3ef055f','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',6,null,null,'spoken','used when something annoying happens in a way that things always seem to happen',null,null,'زمانی استفاده می شود که اتفاق آزاردهنده ای رخ می دهد به گونه ای که به نظر می رسد همیشه اتفاق می افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Of course, it had to happen today, when all the shops are shut.","translation":"البته امروز که همه مغازه ها تعطیل هستند باید این اتفاق می افتاد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020081.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9d77d271-7739-5ca9-8594-c6d358f8357d','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',7,null,null,'spoken','used to say that only one thing or person is good enough or right for someone',null,null,'می گفت فقط یک چیز یا شخص برای کسی خوب یا مناسب است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"For Francesca it has to be the Ritz – nowhere else will do.","translation":"برای فرانچسکا باید Ritz باشد - هیچ جای دیگری این کار را نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001526060.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('10e4206e-3003-50f1-9632-a3b43263992e','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',8,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'do you have to do sth?','داشتن (ویژگی، مالکیت، ارتباط)؛ خوردن؛ فرزند داشتن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('706cfef6-0a7f-55e9-82c1-d26b46e7ee6e','53ed8ea5-f0d7-5086-ac68-19012270dd18',9,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I have to say/admit/confess','داشتن (ویژگی، مالکیت، ارتباط)؛ خوردن؛ فرزند داشتن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1df04cf9-8ddb-5328-9adf-2a730e68e631','27b75a29-8fdd-535e-88c0-4c3a78e88a47',1,'top of body','بالای بدن','spoken & written','the top part of your body that has your face at the front and is supported by your neck','[ countable ]',null,'سر، سرِ (تخت)؛ رأس (صف)؛ سر (افتادن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['turn your head John turned his head to look at the boy.','shake your head (= move it from side to side, especially to show disagreement ) ‘It’s too much, ’ he said, shaking his head.','nod your head (= move it up and down, especially to show agreement ) The audience nodded their heads enthusiastically.','somebody’s head hurts/aches/throbs Her head was throbbing and she needed to lie down.','raise/lift your head (= look up ) Tom raised his head to listen, then went back to his book.','bow/bend/lower your head (= look down ) He bowed his head and tried not not to look at her.','hang your head (= look down, especially because you are ashamed ) She hung her head, not sure how to reply.','scratch your head (= especially because you do not understand something ) He scratched his head and started looking through the drawers again.','cock your head (= hold your head at an angle ) The big dog cocked his head to one side and raised his ears.','bare The sun beat down on her bare head.','bald His bald head shone with sweat.','somebody’s blonde/dark/grey etc head (= with blonde etc hair ) I saw my son’s blond head sticking out from the car window.','head injury Wearing a helmet reduces the risk of head injuries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He kissed the top of her head.","translation":"بالای سرش را بوسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001966854.mp3"},{"sentence":"Alan fell asleep as soon as he put his head on the pillow.","translation":"آلن به محض اینکه سرش را روی بالش گذاشت خوابش برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000754.mp3"},{"sentence":"They dived head first into the water.","translation":"آنها ابتدا سر در آب فرو رفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040084.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was dressed in black from head to toe (= over all her body ) .","translation":"از سر تا پا (= سراسر بدنش) لباس سیاه پوشیده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040085.mp3"},{"sentence":"He still has a full head of hair (= has all his hair, even though he is getting rather old ) .","translation":"او هنوز یک سر پر از مو دارد (= همه موهایش را دارد، با اینکه نسبتاً پیر شده است).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040086.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('47b7cb9a-6c55-51f1-a49e-7e5968c14868','27b75a29-8fdd-535e-88c0-4c3a78e88a47',2,'mind','ذهن','spoken & written','your mind or mental ability','[ countable ]',null,'ذهن یا توانایی ذهنی شما','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['turn your head John turned his head to look at the boy.','shake your head (= move it from side to side, especially to show disagreement ) ‘It’s too much, ’ he said, shaking his head.','nod your head (= move it up and down, especially to show agreement ) The audience nodded their heads enthusiastically.','somebody’s head hurts/aches/throbs Her head was throbbing and she needed to lie down.','raise/lift your head (= look up ) Tom raised his head to listen, then went back to his book.','bow/bend/lower your head (= look down ) He bowed his head and tried not not to look at her.','hang your head (= look down, especially because you are ashamed ) She hung her head, not sure how to reply.','scratch your head (= especially because you do not understand something ) He scratched his head and started looking through the drawers again.','cock your head (= hold your head at an angle ) The big dog cocked his head to one side and raised his ears.','bare The sun beat down on her bare head.','bald His bald head shone with sweat.','somebody’s blonde/dark/grey etc head (= with blonde etc hair ) I saw my son’s blond head sticking out from the car window.','head injury Wearing a helmet reduces the risk of head injuries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The problem only exists inside his head.","translation":"مشکل فقط درون سرش هست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001348691.mp3"},{"sentence":"I can’t do those figures in my head.","translation":"من نمی توانم آن ارقام را در ذهنم انجام دهم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001348695.mp3"},{"sentence":"Use your head to work out the answer.","translation":"از سر خود برای یافتن پاسخ استفاده کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788759.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jackie said the first thing that came into her head.","translation":"جکی اولین چیزی که به ذهنش رسید گفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788764.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘It’s over, Jake, ’ she said. ‘Try and get that into your head.’","translation":"او گفت: «تمام شد، جیک. \"سعی کنید و آن را به ذهن خود بیاورید.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788768.mp3"},{"sentence":"At about two in the morning, Alan took it into his head to go for a swim.","translation":"حدود ساعت دو نیمه شب، آلن آن را به سرش برد تا برای شنا برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788772.mp3"},{"sentence":"Try to put it out of your head for the time being.","translation":"سعی کنید فعلا آن را از ذهن خود خارج کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788776.mp3"},{"sentence":"What’s put that idea into her head?","translation":"چه چیزی این ایده را در سر او گذاشته است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788780.mp3"},{"sentence":"I just can’t get my head round what’s been going on here.","translation":"من نمی توانم متوجه شوم که اینجا چه خبر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788785.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('9bcb16e2-a6bd-56e3-9680-942786f24b18','27b75a29-8fdd-535e-88c0-4c3a78e88a47',3,'calm/sensible','آرام / معقول','informal','to remain calm and sensible in a difficult or frightening situation',null,null,'در یک موقعیت دشوار یا ترسناک آرام و معقول باقی بماند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['turn your head John turned his head to look at the boy.','shake your head (= move it from side to side, especially to show disagreement ) ‘It’s too much, ’ he said, shaking his head.','nod your head (= move it up and down, especially to show agreement ) The audience nodded their heads enthusiastically.','somebody’s head hurts/aches/throbs Her head was throbbing and she needed to lie down.','raise/lift your head (= look up ) Tom raised his head to listen, then went back to his book.','bow/bend/lower your head (= look down ) He bowed his head and tried not not to look at her.','hang your head (= look down, especially because you are ashamed ) She hung her head, not sure how to reply.','scratch your head (= especially because you do not understand something ) He scratched his head and started looking through the drawers again.','cock your head (= hold your head at an angle ) The big dog cocked his head to one side and raised his ears.','bare The sun beat down on her bare head.','bald His bald head shone with sweat.','somebody’s blonde/dark/grey etc head (= with blonde etc hair ) I saw my son’s blond head sticking out from the car window.','head injury Wearing a helmet reduces the risk of head injuries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We need a candidate who can keep his or her head even when clients get aggressive.","translation":"ما به نامزدی نیاز داریم که بتواند سر خود را حفظ کند حتی زمانی که مشتریان پرخاشگر هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788792.mp3"},{"sentence":"Get to sleep early tonight – you’ll need to keep a clear head tomorrow at the trial.","translation":"امشب زود بخوابید - فردا در جلسه محاکمه باید ذهن خود را روشن نگه دارید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788795.mp3"},{"sentence":"You’ll be OK as long as you don’t lose your head and forget he’s the real enemy.","translation":"تا زمانی که سر خود را از دست ندهید و فراموش نکنید که او دشمن واقعی است، خوب خواهید بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788799.mp3"},{"sentence":"He wondered what Gemma thought about it all. She seemed to have her head screwed on.","translation":"او تعجب کرد که جما در مورد این همه چه فکر می کند. به نظر می رسید سرش را به هم زده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788804.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('437b58c8-ee8e-589d-ae8e-d3eca2e69717','27b75a29-8fdd-535e-88c0-4c3a78e88a47',4,'person in charge','مسئول','spoken & written','a leader or person in charge of a group or organization','[ countable ]','crowned head , head boy , head girl , headmaster , headmistress','یک رهبر یا مسئول یک گروه یا سازمان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['turn your head John turned his head to look at the boy.','shake your head (= move it from side to side, especially to show disagreement ) ‘It’s too much, ’ he said, shaking his head.','nod your head (= move it up and down, especially to show agreement ) The audience nodded their heads enthusiastically.','somebody’s head hurts/aches/throbs Her head was throbbing and she needed to lie down.','raise/lift your head (= look up ) Tom raised his head to listen, then went back to his book.','bow/bend/lower your head (= look down ) He bowed his head and tried not not to look at her.','hang your head (= look down, especially because you are ashamed ) She hung her head, not sure how to reply.','scratch your head (= especially because you do not understand something ) He scratched his head and started looking through the drawers again.','cock your head (= hold your head at an angle ) The big dog cocked his head to one side and raised his ears.','bare The sun beat down on her bare head.','bald His bald head shone with sweat.','somebody’s blonde/dark/grey etc head (= with blonde etc hair ) I saw my son’s blond head sticking out from the car window.','head injury Wearing a helmet reduces the risk of head injuries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You should discuss the matter with your head of department.","translation":"شما باید موضوع را با رئیس بخش خود در میان بگذارید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788813.mp3"},{"sentence":"A meeting of Commonwealth heads of state will be held next month.","translation":"نشست سران کشورهای مشترک المنافع ماه آینده برگزار می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788814.mp3"},{"sentence":"From now on all violent incidents should be reported directly to the head.","translation":"از این پس همه حوادث خشونت آمیز باید مستقیماً به رئیس گزارش شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788828.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('567ba702-08fc-5ba4-919a-523ff0367afa','27b75a29-8fdd-535e-88c0-4c3a78e88a47',5,'front/leading position','موقعیت جلو / پیشرو','spoken & written','the front or the most important position','[ singular ]',null,'جلو یا مهمترین موقعیت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['turn your head John turned his head to look at the boy.','shake your head (= move it from side to side, especially to show disagreement ) ‘It’s too much, ’ he said, shaking his head.','nod your head (= move it up and down, especially to show agreement ) The audience nodded their heads enthusiastically.','somebody’s head hurts/aches/throbs Her head was throbbing and she needed to lie down.','raise/lift your head (= look up ) Tom raised his head to listen, then went back to his book.','bow/bend/lower your head (= look down ) He bowed his head and tried not not to look at her.','hang your head (= look down, especially because you are ashamed ) She hung her head, not sure how to reply.','scratch your head (= especially because you do not understand something ) He scratched his head and started looking through the drawers again.','cock your head (= hold your head at an angle ) The big dog cocked his head to one side and raised his ears.','bare The sun beat down on her bare head.','bald His bald head shone with sweat.','somebody’s blonde/dark/grey etc head (= with blonde etc hair ) I saw my son’s blond head sticking out from the car window.','head injury Wearing a helmet reduces the risk of head injuries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Jenny marched proudly at the head of the procession.","translation":"جنی با افتخار در رأس موکب راهپیمایی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788843.mp3"},{"sentence":"At the head of the table (= the place where the most important person sits ) sat the senior partners.","translation":"سر میز (= مکانی که مهمترین فرد در آن می نشیند) شرکای ارشد نشسته اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788844.mp3"},{"sentence":"The band of soldiers marched into the yard, their defeated captain at their head.","translation":"گروه سربازان در حالی که کاپیتان شکست خورده خود را در سر داشتند وارد حیاط شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788850.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1f8a5d13-53de-5d86-81ab-dc5e2a03e978','27b75a29-8fdd-535e-88c0-4c3a78e88a47',6,'crazy','دیوانه','spoken & written','used in particular phrases to talk about someone being crazy or very stupid','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'در عبارات خاصی برای صحبت در مورد دیوانه یا بسیار احمق بودن شخصی استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['turn your head John turned his head to look at the boy.','shake your head (= move it from side to side, especially to show disagreement ) ‘It’s too much, ’ he said, shaking his head.','nod your head (= move it up and down, especially to show agreement ) The audience nodded their heads enthusiastically.','somebody’s head hurts/aches/throbs Her head was throbbing and she needed to lie down.','raise/lift your head (= look up ) Tom raised his head to listen, then went back to his book.','bow/bend/lower your head (= look down ) He bowed his head and tried not not to look at her.','hang your head (= look down, especially because you are ashamed ) She hung her head, not sure how to reply.','scratch your head (= especially because you do not understand something ) He scratched his head and started looking through the drawers again.','cock your head (= hold your head at an angle ) The big dog cocked his head to one side and raised his ears.','bare The sun beat down on her bare head.','bald His bald head shone with sweat.','somebody’s blonde/dark/grey etc head (= with blonde etc hair ) I saw my son’s blond head sticking out from the car window.','head injury Wearing a helmet reduces the risk of head injuries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"People going out in conditions like this need their heads examined .","translation":"افرادی که در چنین شرایطی بیرون می روند باید سر خود را معاینه کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788859.mp3"},{"sentence":"You must be off your head if you think that.","translation":"اگر این فکر را می کنید، باید از سر خود بی خبر باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788863.mp3"},{"sentence":"If I walk in looking like that, they’ll think I’m not right in the head .","translation":"اگر من به این شکل وارد شوم، آنها فکر می کنند که من در ذهنم درست نیستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001788864.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
