('b3c3405f-e48e-5c56-8c42-40f94e896b92','72d169e8-03b2-588e-a5a4-85a85ab648fd',5,'electronic equipment','تجهیزات الکترونیکی','spoken & written','to connect a piece of electronic equipment to another piece of equipment or to an electricity supply','[ always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'برای اتصال یک قطعه از تجهیزات الکترونیکی به یک قطعه دیگر از تجهیزات یا به منبع برق','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’ve got a CD player, but it’s not hooked up yet.","translation":"ما یک دستگاه پخش سی دی داریم، اما هنوز وصل نشده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745482.mp3"},{"sentence":"Computers from different manufacturers can often be hooked together.","translation":"رایانه های تولید کنندگان مختلف اغلب می توانند به یکدیگر متصل شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745479.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('24aaf744-81cc-568e-9cf6-fd0dc41a2d80','72d169e8-03b2-588e-a5a4-85a85ab648fd',6,'ball','توپ','spoken & written','to throw or kick a ball so that it moves in a curve',null,null,'پرتاب یا لگد زدن به یک توپ به طوری که در یک منحنی حرکت کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('dac46f70-1136-56e2-98d8-6accd47e4b49','0098b44c-b9f6-572f-9d89-af28a3850e94',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to want something to happen or be true and to believe that it is possible or likely',null,null,'امید داشتن، آرزو کردن؛ (امید) چشم‌داشت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We hope that more women will decide to join the course.","translation":"امیدواریم زنان بیشتری تصمیم بگیرند که در این دوره شرکت کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745578.mp3"},{"sentence":"I do hope everything goes well.","translation":"امیدوارم همه چیز خوب پیش بره","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745579.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was hoped that the job would be filled by a local person.","translation":"امید می رفت که این شغل توسط یک فرد محلی پر شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745580.mp3"},{"sentence":"Let’s just hope someone finds her bag.","translation":"فقط امیدوار باشیم کسی کیفش را پیدا کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745581.mp3"},{"sentence":"I hope to God I haven’t left the car window open.","translation":"به خدا امیدوارم شیشه ماشین رو باز نگذاشته باشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745586.mp3"},{"sentence":"Joan’s hoping to study law at Harvard.","translation":"جوآن امیدوار است در هاروارد حقوق بخواند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745591.mp3"},{"sentence":"We were hoping for good weather.","translation":"ما به هوای خوب امیدوار بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001359520.mp3"},{"sentence":"Liam decided to ignore the warning and just hope for the best (= hope that a situation will end well when there is a risk of things going wrong ) .","translation":"لیام تصمیم گرفت اخطار را نادیده بگیرد و فقط به بهترین ها امیدوار باشد (= امیدواریم که یک وضعیت به خوبی پایان یابد وقتی خطر خراب شدن چیزها وجود دارد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745592.mp3"},{"sentence":"I rang my parents, hoping against hope (= hoping for something that is very unlikely to happen or be true ) that they hadn’t left yet.","translation":"من به والدینم زنگ زدم، به امید امید (= به امید چیزی که احتمال وقوع یا واقعی بودن آن بسیار کم است) که هنوز آن را ترک نکرده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745597.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('0e17aa02-de83-5b35-a783-fa68e772e5a2','0098b44c-b9f6-572f-9d89-af28a3850e94',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I hope so','امید داشتن، آرزو کردن؛ (امید) چشم‌داشت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f372febc-e626-5fd7-ab2d-3384ec14fa0e','0098b44c-b9f6-572f-9d89-af28a3850e94',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I hope not','امید داشتن، آرزو کردن؛ (امید) چشم‌داشت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d89b84eb-eaa8-513f-b45f-6bfff00821f7','0098b44c-b9f6-572f-9d89-af28a3850e94',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I’m hoping','امید داشتن، آرزو کردن؛ (امید) چشم‌داشت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('62360925-9fc0-5794-997f-8fc8bb6004ab','0098b44c-b9f6-572f-9d89-af28a3850e94',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I hope (that)','امید داشتن، آرزو کردن؛ (امید) چشم‌داشت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fcb6e2c4-3871-55a7-9a26-31df87ea9838','0098b44c-b9f6-572f-9d89-af28a3850e94',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I should hope so (too)','امید داشتن، آرزو کردن؛ (امید) چشم‌داشت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8e990c71-5004-5349-9009-bd4e5ba8199d','55a271a1-82f9-5f7e-be1b-cdfccb3e29f3',1,'feeling','احساس','spoken & written','a feeling of wanting something to happen or be true and believing that it is possible or likely','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'امید، امیدواری؛ امکان (شاید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have hope The situation looked bad, but we still had hope that things would get better soon.','give/offer hope The research has given hope to thousands of sufferers of the disease.','lose/give up/abandon hope (= stop hoping ) After so long without any word from David, Margaret was starting to lose hope.','raise somebody’s hopes ( also get/build somebody''s hopes up ) (= make someone feel that what they want is likely to happen ) I don''t want to raise your hopes too much. Don’t build your hopes up, Julie. You’ll only get hurt.','hold out hope (= say that you think something is likely ) Negotiators did not hold out much hope of a peaceful solution.','pin your hopes on something (= hope for one thing that everything else depends on ) After a difficult year, the company is pinning its hopes on its new range of products.','cling to the hope that (= keep hoping that something will happen, even though it seems unlikely ) They clung to the hope that one day a cure would be found.','dash/shatter somebody’s hopes (= make what someone wants seem impossible ) The ending of the talks has dashed any hopes of peace.','hopes are fading (= people have much less hope of doing something ) Hopes are fading that rescuers will find any more survivors.','hope lies in/with something (= something gives people hope ) Our real hope lies with a vaccine.','be full of hope His voice sounded full of hope.','a glimmer/ray of hope (= a little hope, or something that gives you a little hope ) The new treatment gives patients a glimmer of hope.','somebody’s hopes and dreams (= all the things someone hopes for ) We talked about all our hopes and dreams for the future.','somebody’s hopes and fears (= all the things someone hopes for and is afraid of ) The crew members have different hopes and fears about the trip.','it is our fervent hope that formal (= used when saying that you hope very much that something will or will not happen ) It is our fervent hope that change is coming.','hope springs eternal (= used to say that people will always hope for something ) It is unlikely these diets will work, but hope springs eternal.','a symbol/beacon of hope (= something that makes people have hope ) Mandela was a symbol of hope for his whole country.','false hope We don''t want to give people false hopes.','a vain/forlorn hope (= hope for something that is impossible ) He traveled south in the vain hope of finding work.','somebody''s only/one hope My only hope is that someone may have handed in the keys to the police.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"When I first arrived in New York, I was full of hope for the future.","translation":"وقتی برای اولین بار وارد نیویورک شدم، به آینده پر امید بودم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040090.mp3"},{"sentence":"The president has expressed the hope that relations will improve.","translation":"رئیس جمهور ابراز امیدواری کرده است که روابط بهبود یابد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967133.mp3"},{"sentence":"hopes for an end to the fighting","translation":"به پایان جنگ امیدوار است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040091.mp3"},{"sentence":"Rita has hopes of studying to be a nurse.","translation":"ریتا امیدوار است که پرستاری کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967140.mp3"},{"sentence":"Should they hang on in the hope that the shares will go up in value?","translation":"آیا آنها باید به امید افزایش ارزش سهام ادامه دهند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040092.mp3"},{"sentence":"Shoppers flocked to the sales in the hope of finding a bargain.","translation":"خریداران به امید یافتن یک معامله به سمت فروش هجوم آوردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040093.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('1d23b957-9f8d-55b1-b6ce-616877a7c6e7','55a271a1-82f9-5f7e-be1b-cdfccb3e29f3',2,'something you hope for','چیزی که بهش امیدواری','spoken & written','something that you hope will happen','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که امیدوارید اتفاق بیفتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have hope The situation looked bad, but we still had hope that things would get better soon.','give/offer hope The research has given hope to thousands of sufferers of the disease.','lose/give up/abandon hope (= stop hoping ) After so long without any word from David, Margaret was starting to lose hope.','raise somebody’s hopes ( also get/build somebody''s hopes up ) (= make someone feel that what they want is likely to happen ) I don''t want to raise your hopes too much. Don’t build your hopes up, Julie. You’ll only get hurt.','hold out hope (= say that you think something is likely ) Negotiators did not hold out much hope of a peaceful solution.','pin your hopes on something (= hope for one thing that everything else depends on ) After a difficult year, the company is pinning its hopes on its new range of products.','cling to the hope that (= keep hoping that something will happen, even though it seems unlikely ) They clung to the hope that one day a cure would be found.','dash/shatter somebody’s hopes (= make what someone wants seem impossible ) The ending of the talks has dashed any hopes of peace.','hopes are fading (= people have much less hope of doing something ) Hopes are fading that rescuers will find any more survivors.','hope lies in/with something (= something gives people hope ) Our real hope lies with a vaccine.','be full of hope His voice sounded full of hope.','a glimmer/ray of hope (= a little hope, or something that gives you a little hope ) The new treatment gives patients a glimmer of hope.','somebody’s hopes and dreams (= all the things someone hopes for ) We talked about all our hopes and dreams for the future.','somebody’s hopes and fears (= all the things someone hopes for and is afraid of ) The crew members have different hopes and fears about the trip.','it is our fervent hope that formal (= used when saying that you hope very much that something will or will not happen ) It is our fervent hope that change is coming.','hope springs eternal (= used to say that people will always hope for something ) It is unlikely these diets will work, but hope springs eternal.','a symbol/beacon of hope (= something that makes people have hope ) Mandela was a symbol of hope for his whole country.','false hope We don''t want to give people false hopes.','a vain/forlorn hope (= hope for something that is impossible ) He traveled south in the vain hope of finding work.','somebody''s only/one hope My only hope is that someone may have handed in the keys to the police.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She told him all her secret hopes and fears.","translation":"او تمام امیدها و ترس های پنهان خود را به او گفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001360163.mp3"},{"sentence":"My hope is that by next summer I’ll have saved enough money to go travelling.","translation":"امیدوارم تا تابستان آینده پول کافی برای رفتن به سفر پس انداز کرده باشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745652.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('491614b3-d122-5853-a949-2608d1ae073d','55a271a1-82f9-5f7e-be1b-cdfccb3e29f3',3,'chance','شانس','spoken','a chance of succeeding or of something good happening','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'شانس موفقیت یا اتفاق خوب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It was the rush hour, and there was no hope of getting a seat.","translation":"ساعت شلوغی بود و هیچ امیدی به نشستن نبود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040094.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was a desperate plan, with little hope of success.","translation":"این یک طرح ناامیدکننده بود، با امید به موفقیت کمی.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745653.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s still a faint hope (= a very small chance ) that the two sides will reach an agreement.","translation":"هنوز امید ضعیفی (= شانس بسیار کم) وجود دارد که دو طرف به توافق برسند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001745656.mp3"},{"sentence":"They don’t have a hope in hell of winning.","translation":"آنها امیدی به جهنم بردن ندارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001360222.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Your dad might lend you the car.’ ‘Some hope!’","translation":"«ممکن است پدرت ماشین را به تو قرض دهد.» «کمی امید!»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001360228.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
